 meets target?Target AchievedTarget Not AchievedDisplay cost and profit reportStopYesNo

## 4. Python Source Code

```
material = float(input("Enter material cost: Rs. "))labour = float(input("Enter labour charges: Rs. "))machine = float(input("Enter machine cost: Rs. "))wastage_percent = float(input("Enter wastage percentage: "))units = int(input("Enter units produced: "))selling_price = float(input("Enter selling price per unit: Rs. "))target = float(input("Enter target profit: Rs. "))wastage = material * wastage_percent / 100total_cost = material + labour + machine + wastagerevenue = units * selling_priceprofit = revenue - total_costif total_cost > 0:    profit_percent = profit / total_cost * 100else:    profit_percent = 0print("\n===== MANUFACTURING REPORT =====")print(f"Material Cost : Rs. {material:.2f}")print(f"Labour Cost   : Rs. {labour:.2f}")print(f"Machine Cost  : Rs. {machine:.2f}")print(f"Wastage Cost  : Rs. {wastage:.2f}")print(f"Total Cost    : Rs. {total_cost:.2f}")print(f"Total Revenue : Rs. {revenue:.2f}")print(f"Profit/Loss   : Rs. {profit:.2f}")print(f"Profit Margin : {profit_percent:.2f}%")if profit >= target:    print("Result: Profit target achieved")else:    print("Result: Profit target not achieved")
```

## 5. Sample Input

```
Enter material cost: Rs. 10000
Enter labour charges: Rs. 3000
Enter machine cost: Rs. 2000
Enter wastage percentage: 5
Enter units produced: 100
Enter selling price per unit: Rs. 200
Enter target profit: Rs. 3000
```

## 6. Sample Output

```
===== MANUFACTURING REPORT =====
Material Cost : Rs. 10000.00
Labour Cost   : Rs. 3000.00
Machine Cost  : Rs. 2000.00
Wastage Cost  : Rs. 500.00
Total Cost    : Rs. 15500.00
Total Revenue : Rs. 20000.00
Profit/Loss   : Rs. 4500.00
Profit Margin : 29.03%
Result: Profit target achieved
```

## 7. Result

The program calculates manufacturing expenses, wastage, revenue, profit or loss, and profit percentage. It also determines whether the specified profit target is achieved.
